new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1d8e3a0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static page; run `npm test` for the origin validation regression tests. No build is required.
+
+The ordering integration assumes `https://orders.dailygrind.coffee` is controlled by
+the operator. Set `ORDERING_ORIGIN` in `origin-validation.mjs` and the Order Now link
+in `index.html` to the real service before deployment. The service opens at
+`/order-online` and may send `{ type: 'order-complete' }` or
+`{ type: 'redirect', url: '...' }` to its opener. Messages require both the opened
+window and the exact trusted origin. Redirects must be schemeful same-site with
+the page and contain no credentials.
+
+Where supported, the native `Origin` API supplies Public Suffix List site checks
+and opaque sandbox identity. Without it, same-site validation permits the current
+origin and subdomains of the explicitly controlled `dailygrind.coffee` domain
+(`SITE_DOMAIN`). Other deployments conservatively allow only the current origin;
+do not replace this with hostname splitting for arbitrary domains. External HTTP(S)
+links remain usable with `noopener noreferrer`; non-web links are blocked.
+
+The widget pins its opaque sender origin once, on `init`, and always checks its
+captured source window. Without `Origin`, the source window is the identity
+boundary; browsers cannot expose opaque document identity across navigation in
+that fallback. The widget has only `allow-scripts`, sends no customer data, and
+cannot navigate its parent. A reloaded widget with a new opaque identity requires
+reinitializing the parent validator (reloading the page).
+
+Tests exercise URL attacks and sandbox identity contracts using Node, including
+an `Origin` test double. They do not assert real browser support for that API.
